# A PDF's cross-reference table records the byte offset of every object, so a
# single rewritten line ending corrupts the whole file. Git only treats a file
# as binary when it finds a NUL byte, and the demo PDFs under
# public/mocks/documentos/ are plain-text PDFs without one — with
# core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout would convert their LFs to CRLF and
# shift every offset. `binary` turns off end-of-line conversion and text diffs.
*.pdf binary
